    "tweet1": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "1/ aaronjmars/aeon crossed 500 GitHub stars today. 21 days after hitting 400. The 300→400 gap was 6 days — that was launch week. This is the organic rate."
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "tweet2": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "2/ The first 200 stars came fast — launch momentum, social push, a spike. Then it held. 26 stars a week over the last 7 days, 207 over the last 30. No collapse after the initial burst."
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "tweet3": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "3/ This week the codebase gained provider-agnostic routing: a gateway that cascades across 7 LLM providers on any failure. Claude down, out of credits, rate-limited — the agent keeps running."
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "tweet4": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "4/ LLM provider concentration is a real production risk. Most agent frameworks are wired to one API and stop dead when it does. 500 stars says people are noticing a framework that isn't."
      },
      "children": []
    },
